{"name":"California Stucco","hex":"#c5ad9a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stucco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A material with binder and aggregate that is used to coat interior walls or to make interior mouldings.","A material with binder and aggregate that is used to coat exterior walls or to make exterior mouldings."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To coat or decorate with stucco."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stucco"}],"entries":[{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California","wikidata":"Q99"},{"title":"Stucco","blocks":[{"text":"Stucco or render is a construction material made of aggregates, a binder, and water. Stucco is applied wet and hardens to a very dense solid. It is most commonly used as a decorative and protective cladding for exterior walls and canopies. Stucco can be applied over construction materials such as metal, expanded metal lath, concrete, cinder block, or clay brick and adobe for decorative, protective or structural purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Ceilings_of_the_rotonde_de_Mars_%28509%29.jpg/330px-Ceilings_of_the_rotonde_de_Mars_%28509%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stucco","wikidata":"Q33526"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia